    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/page-head {\"eyebrow\":\"All faiths and backgrounds · Six languages\",\"title\":\"Religious and cultural circumcision in London\",\"lede\":\"Religious and cultural circumcision is a large part of our day-to-day work at Beverley Clinic.\",\"reviewedBy\":\"\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/team/#haidar\\u0022\\u003eDr Haidar Al-Ali, BDS, MFDS RCPS (Glasg)\\u003c/a\\u003e, September 2026\",\"crumbs\":[{\"label\":\"Who we see\",\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\"},{\"label\":\"Religious and cultural\",\"href\":\"\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section-sm\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section-sm\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:html --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Religious and cultural circumcision is a large part of our day-to-day work at Beverley Clinic.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We welcome babies, children, teenagers and adults from all faiths, cultures and backgrounds and understand that circumcision can have an important religious, cultural and family significance beyond the procedure itself.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our practitioners have extensive experience performing circumcision across different age groups. Our Muslim practitioners can provide circumcision for Muslim families who wish their son to be circumcised in accordance with their religious beliefs and traditions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We also welcome Jewish families and patients from African, Filipino, Fijian and other communities where male circumcision is traditionally or culturally practised.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whatever your reason for choosing circumcision, the same clinical standards apply: assessment before treatment, an age-appropriate circumcision technique, local anaesthetic, detailed aftercare and follow-up support during healing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:cil/spec-panel {\"eyebrow\":\"Practical detail\",\"rows\":[{\"k\":\"Sunnah practice\",\"v\":\"Yes, by our Muslim practitioners\"},{\"k\":\"All faiths\",\"v\":\"Families and adult patients welcome\"},{\"k\":\"Anaesthetic\",\"v\":\"Local anaesthetic\"},{\"k\":\"Aftercare\",\"v\":\"Written aftercare and follow-up support\"},{\"k\":\"Languages\",\"v\":\"English, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish\"},{\"k\":\"Setting\",\"v\":\"CQC registered clinic\"}],\"note\":\"\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"faiths-and-traditions\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"faiths-and-traditions\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Faiths \\u0026 traditions\",\"heading\":\"Circumcision across different faiths and cultures\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Sunnah practice\",\"title\":\"Muslim and Sunnah circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision, known as Khitan, is an important religious practice for many Muslim families.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe understand that parents may want their son's circumcision to respect both their religious beliefs and appropriate clinical standards.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur Muslim practitioners regularly perform circumcisions for Muslim families and understand the religious importance of the procedure.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFamilies from different Muslim communities may have different traditions concerning the timing of circumcision. Some choose circumcision during the first few weeks or months of life, while others prefer to wait until their son is older.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFrom a clinical perspective, the technique we use depends primarily on the child's age, anatomy and individual circumstances rather than religious background.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and younger children, we commonly use the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method where clinically suitable.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor older children, teenagers and adults, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eLocal anaesthetic is used for circumcisions performed at our clinic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Jewish community\",\"title\":\"Jewish circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWe also welcome Jewish patients and families seeking circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe recognise that circumcision has an important religious significance within Judaism and that individual families may have specific requirements regarding how and when the circumcision takes place.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur service is a clinical circumcision service, so Jewish families with specific religious or ceremonial requirements should discuss these with us before booking. This allows us to explain what we can provide within our clinical setting and ensure that the arrangements meet your needs.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Global communities\",\"title\":\"Circumcision as a cultural tradition\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision is practised for cultural as well as religious reasons in many communities around the world.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe regularly see families and adult patients whose decision to circumcise is connected to their family or cultural background.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis includes patients from African, Filipino, Fijian and other communities where male circumcision may traditionally be performed during infancy, childhood, adolescence or adulthood.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe respect these traditions while ensuring that the procedure is approached as a surgical procedure requiring appropriate assessment, anaesthesia, hygiene, consent and aftercare.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"timing-and-age-groups\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"timing-and-age-groups\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Age groups\",\"heading\":\"Circumcision timing and age groups\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Infancy\",\"title\":\"When should a Muslim baby be circumcised?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eDifferent Muslim families and communities have different traditions regarding the timing of circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFrom a clinical perspective, where parents have already decided to circumcise their baby, we generally recommend having the procedure during the first few weeks of life where possible.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eYounger babies are usually suitable for the Plastibell or Circumplast ring technique, subject to examination.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eHowever, there is no need to worry if your son is already older. We regularly circumcise babies, toddlers, children, teenagers and adult men.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe assess each patient individually and select a method appropriate to his age and anatomy.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about baby circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Childhood \\u0026 adolescence\",\"title\":\"Religious circumcision for older boys\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eNot every family chooses circumcision during infancy.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe regularly see older children whose parents have chosen to have them circumcised for religious or cultural reasons.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor older boys, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery under local anaesthetic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe understand that an older child may be anxious about the procedure. Our practitioners are experienced in talking to children and explaining what will happen in an age-appropriate and reassuring way.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe recommend keeping explanations simple, truthful and appropriate for your son's age rather than giving him unnecessary detail that may increase anxiety.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eSchool-holiday appointments are particularly popular because they allow children additional time to recover before returning to school.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about circumcision for children and teenagers →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Eighteen \\u0026 over\",\"title\":\"Religious circumcision for adults\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eSome men choose to be circumcised as adults because of their religious beliefs, cultural background or following conversion to a faith where circumcision is important to them.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe provide adult circumcision in a private and respectful clinical environment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eAdult circumcision is normally performed under local anaesthetic using a forceps-guided technique with thermal cautery. Depending on the individual wound, dissolvable stitches, medical skin glue, a combination of both, or occasionally neither may be used.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe understand that the reasons for choosing adult religious circumcision can be very personal. You are welcome to discuss any religious, cultural or practical requirements with us before booking.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about adult circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"clinical-environment\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"clinical-environment\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Clinical standard\",\"heading\":\"A religious procedure in a clinical environment\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:html --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Religious or cultural circumcision is sometimes described as \"non-medical circumcision\" because there may be no medical condition requiring the foreskin to be removed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>However, the circumcision itself is still a surgical procedure.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At Beverley Clinic, religious and cultural circumcision is therefore approached with the same clinical care as a circumcision performed for medical reasons.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This includes:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} -->\n<ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\">\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Review of relevant medical history</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Examination of the penis and foreskin</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Appropriate consent</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Local anaesthetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>An age-appropriate circumcision technique</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Attention to infection prevention</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Written aftercare instructions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>A next-day follow-up call</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Access to follow-up during healing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n</ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p style=\"margin-top:24px\">Being performed for religious or cultural reasons does not mean that clinical standards should be any different.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\" style=\"margin-top:36px\">What happens before the circumcision?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every patient is assessed before the procedure.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For a baby or child, we ask about his general health and relevant medical history and examine the penis before proceeding.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We look for anything that may affect whether or how circumcision should be performed, including hypospadias, buried penis, unusual anatomy or other clinical concerns.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We also ask about any known bleeding disorder or family history of unusual or excessive bleeding.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If we identify something that means routine circumcision should be delayed or reconsidered, we will explain this to you rather than simply proceeding because the circumcision has been requested for religious reasons.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The safety and best interests of the patient remain our priority.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group --><!-- /wp:html --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"methods-and-anaesthetic\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"methods-and-anaesthetic\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Surgical methods\",\"heading\":\"What circumcision method do you use?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:html --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We do not use the same circumcision technique for every patient.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group --><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Ring method\",\"title\":\"Babies and younger children\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWhere clinically suitable, we commonly use the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eA correctly sized plastic ring is placed underneath the foreskin and the foreskin is secured around it. The unwanted foreskin and ring then separate naturally during healing.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eStitches are not required with this method.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about baby circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Forceps-guided\",\"title\":\"Older children and teenagers\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor older children and teenagers, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eDepending on the patient's age, anatomy and wound, closure may involve dissolvable stitches, medical skin glue, both, or occasionally neither.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about child circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Thermal cautery\",\"title\":\"Adults\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eAdult religious and cultural circumcision is also commonly performed using our forceps-guided technique with thermal cautery under local anaesthetic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about adult circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Individual anatomy\",\"title\":\"Why don't we use the same method for everyone?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe patient's religion or culture does not determine which surgical technique is safest or most appropriate.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe consider age, anatomy, foreskin development and findings on examination before deciding which method to use.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis is why two members of the same family may sometimes have their circumcisions performed using different techniques if they are different ages or have different anatomy.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Pain control\",\"title\":\"Is local anaesthetic used for religious circumcision?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Circumcisions performed at our clinic are carried out using local anaesthetic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe anaesthetic is administered and given time to work before the procedure begins. We check the area before proceeding.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eReligious or cultural reasons for circumcision do not change our approach to pain control.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"consent-and-ethics\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"consent-and-ethics\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Consent \\u0026 ethics\",\"heading\":\"Consent and the child's perspective\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Parental consent\",\"title\":\"Consent for religious circumcision in children\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision is permanent, so appropriate consent is particularly important when the procedure is being chosen for a child who does not have a medical condition requiring surgery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe ask families to provide the identification and consent documentation required by the clinic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor children, we require both parents to with parental responsibility to provide written consent. If you are a single parent, please inform us before booking so that we can advise you on the next steps.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOlder children and teenagers should also be involved in discussions about their circumcision in a way that reflects their age, maturity and understanding.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf parents disagree about whether their child should be circumcised, or there is uncertainty about parental responsibility, contact us before making an appointment. We will not proceed until the consent position has been clarified.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Patient's view\",\"title\":\"What if my child does not want to be circumcised?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eAs children become older, their understanding and views become increasingly important.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf an older child is extremely distressed, actively refuses the procedure or cannot cooperate safely, we will not simply ignore this because the circumcision has been requested for religious or cultural reasons.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe will discuss the situation with the parents and child and decide whether it is appropriate to proceed, postpone the procedure or consider another approach.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur responsibility is to the patient as well as to the family requesting the circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"appointment-preparation\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"appointment-preparation\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Appointment day\",\"heading\":\"Practical arrangements and attendance\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:html --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">What should we bring?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The exact requirements depend on the patient's age.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For babies and children, we may ask you to bring:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} -->\n<ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\">\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The identification and consent documents requested by the clinic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Your child's Red Book where applicable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Birth certificate or passport where available</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Details of medication and medical conditions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Relevant medical letters</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>For babies, clean nappies, wipes and feeding supplies</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Comfortable clothing for older children</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n</ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p style=\"margin-top:20px;margin-bottom:32px\">We will explain the exact requirements when your appointment is booked.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group --><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Family members\",\"title\":\"Can family members attend?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWe understand that circumcision can be an important family occasion.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eHowever, we are also a working clinical environment and need to maintain privacy, safety and sufficient space for staff and patients.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf additional family members would like to attend, particularly where you are planning something around the religious or cultural significance of the circumcision, please discuss this with us before the appointment rather than assuming that a large group can be accommodated.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Religious adviser\",\"title\":\"Can a religious adviser attend?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eIf you would like a religious adviser or another person to be involved for religious reasons, contact us before booking.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe can discuss what may be possible while maintaining the clinical environment, patient privacy, infection-control requirements and the safe conduct of the procedure.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Languages\",\"title\":\"What languages are spoken at the clinic?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eOur team speaks several languages, including:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eEnglish, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor many families, being able to discuss the procedure and aftercare in a familiar language makes the process easier.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf English is not your first language, tell us when arranging your appointment and we will let you know whether a suitable member of the team is available.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"aftercare-and-travel\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"aftercare-and-travel\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Aftercare \\u0026 travel\",\"heading\":\"Recovery, aftercare and travelling home\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Aftercare\",\"title\":\"What happens after the circumcision?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBefore you leave the clinic, we explain how to care for the circumcision at home and provide written aftercare information.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe aftercare depends on the patient's age and the circumcision method used.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor example, parents of a baby who has had a Plastibell or Circumplast circumcision need different instructions from an adult recovering from a forceps-guided circumcision with stitches.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe therefore give you instructions appropriate to the actual procedure performed.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe also make a next-day follow-up call and provide access to follow-up support during the healing period.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/aftercare/\\u0022\\u003eRead our circumcision aftercare information →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Local travel\",\"title\":\"Can we travel home after the circumcision?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eMost patients go home shortly after their circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFamilies regularly travel to us from across London and further afield.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf you are travelling a long distance within the UK or coming from overseas, contact us before booking. We can discuss the patient's age, timing of travel, aftercare and what arrangements you should make in case a review is required.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor patients travelling internationally, it is particularly important to consider how long you will remain locally after the procedure and how follow-up will be managed once you return home.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:html --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"},\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"36px\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"margin-top:36px\">\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">Patients travelling from abroad</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We see patients and families who travel to London specifically for circumcision.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you are travelling from another country, please contact us before arranging flights or accommodation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We can discuss:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} -->\n<ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\">\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The patient's age</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The likely circumcision method</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Medical history</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Documents required</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Appointment timing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>How long you should remain in the UK</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Aftercare</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>What to do if you have concerns after returning home</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n</ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p style=\"margin-top:20px\">Do not arrange your return journey so tightly that there is no opportunity for review if one is required.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group --><!-- /wp:html --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"medical-pricing-location\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"medical-pricing-location\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Safety \\u0026 details\",\"heading\":\"Medical considerations, pricing and clinic location\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Underlying conditions\",\"title\":\"What if my son has a medical problem as well?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eA circumcision requested for religious reasons can sometimes reveal a medical or anatomical issue during assessment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eFor example, a patient may also have phimosis, BXO, a tight frenulum or buried penis.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis can influence the technique, aftercare and sometimes the price of treatment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf you already know that your son has a foreskin or penile problem, tell us before booking so that we can advise you appropriately.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Clinical safety\",\"title\":\"When might we postpone or advise against circumcision?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWe will not automatically perform a circumcision simply because it has religious or cultural importance to the family.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe may postpone or advise against routine circumcision if:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eThe baby or child is unwell\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eThere is a known or suspected bleeding disorder\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eThere is a significant family history of abnormal bleeding\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eCertain types of hypospadias or another anatomical condition is suspected\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eThe anatomy requires further specialist assessment\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eAn older child cannot safely cooperate with the procedure\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eAppropriate consent has not been obtained\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eThere is another clinical reason why the practitioner believes treatment should be delayed\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf we advise you not to proceed, we will explain the reason and what we recommend doing next.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Transparent fees\",\"title\":\"How much does religious circumcision cost?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe price is based primarily on the patient's age and the complexity of the procedure, rather than whether the reason is religious, cultural or personal.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eMore complex cases or patients with an additional medical or foreskin problem may require individual assessment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/prices/\\u0022\\u003eSee our full circumcision price list →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Edgware clinic\",\"title\":\"Religious circumcision in North-West London\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eOur clinic is located at:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eBeverley Clinic, 78 Beverley Drive, Edgware, North-West London, HA8 5NE\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe see Muslim, Jewish and other religious and cultural communities from across London, the wider UK and overseas.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe clinic has good public transport connections and parking nearby.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf you are travelling a significant distance, contact us before booking so that we can discuss the practical arrangements.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"certificates\",\"caption\":\"Qualifications hang in the corridor. Ask to see any of them.\",\"alt\":\"Framed qualifications along the clinic corridor at the Edgware practice.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/callback-card {\"eyebrow\":\"Request a call back\",\"title\":\"Ask us first\",\"formId\":\"religious\",\"subject\":\"religious and cultural circumcision enquiry\",\"urgent\":false} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"Frequently asked questions about religious circumcision\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Do you provide Muslim circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Religious circumcision is a significant part of our work, and our Muslim practitioners regularly perform circumcisions for Muslim babies, children, teenagers and adults.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you perform circumcision according to the Sunnah?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eOur Muslim practitioners understand the religious importance of circumcision within Islam. If your family has a particular religious requirement, discuss it with us before booking so that we can confirm what we can provide within our clinical setting.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What age should a Muslim boy be circumcised?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eDifferent Muslim families and communities follow different traditions. From a clinical perspective, where parents have already decided to circumcise, we generally recommend the first few weeks of life where possible. We also regularly circumcise older babies, children, teenagers and adults.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you welcome Jewish patients?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Jewish patients and families are welcome. If you require particular religious or ceremonial arrangements, contact us before booking so that we can discuss whether these can be accommodated within our clinical service.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you circumcise adults who have converted to Islam or Judaism?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. We see adult patients choosing circumcision for religious reasons, including men who have converted to Islam or Judaism. The consultation and treatment are private and respectful.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Is religious circumcision performed with anaesthetic?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Circumcisions at our clinic are performed using local anaesthetic.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Is the procedure different for religious circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe reason for circumcision does not by itself determine the surgical method. The technique is selected according to the patient's age, anatomy and clinical assessment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can my baby have a Plastibell circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eMany babies and toddlers are suitable for a Plastibell or Circumplast ring circumcision. We examine the child first and select the method and ring size we consider appropriate.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can an older child be circumcised under local anaesthetic?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eMany suitable older children and teenagers are treated under local anaesthetic at our clinic. We also consider the child's maturity, anxiety and ability to cooperate safely.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do both parents need to agree to a child's religious circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBecause non-medically necessary circumcision is permanent, consent and parental responsibility need to be clear before treatment. Therefore, both biological parents are required to consent. If you are a single parent or there are alterative child arrangement orders, please contact us with more information before booking.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What if the parents disagree?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eTell us before booking. We will not proceed while there is an unresolved disagreement about consent for a child's religious or cultural circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can relatives come to the appointment?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003ePossibly, but numbers may need to be limited because this is a clinical environment. Contact us beforehand if additional family members would like to attend.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can a religious adviser attend?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eDiscuss this with us before booking. We can explain what can be accommodated while maintaining patient safety, privacy and appropriate clinical conditions. If we do allow, it will only be in the waiting room and not inside the surgery room.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you provide aftercare?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Patients and parents receive detailed aftercare information, a next-day follow-up call and access to follow-up support during healing.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can we travel from outside London?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. We regularly see patients from outside London. If you are travelling a long distance, contact us beforehand so that we can discuss timing and follow-up.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you see international patients?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. If you are travelling from overseas, contact us before arranging travel so that we can discuss the procedure, documentation, how long you should remain locally and arrangements for follow-up.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-band {\"eyebrow\":\"Talk to us\",\"title\":\"Ask about a date\",\"text\":\"If you are travelling a long distance, contact us before booking so we can discuss timing, documentation and follow-up arrangements.\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book a consultation\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"By age\",\"heading\":\"The procedure itself, by age group\",\"lede\":\"\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/group-cards {\"level\":3,\"exclude\":\"\",\"banded\":false} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->"
}
